description:
Change under review. Task: `sessions list --since <date>` shows only the sessions that started on or after that date. Acceptance: without `--since` every session is listed; with it, sessions that started before the date are left out; `filterSessions` is covered by tests for both.

Added files are shown in full. For changed files, only the changed region is shown; the rest of the file is unchanged and compiles.

`src/sessions/filter.ts` (added):
```ts
1 import type { Session } from "./types.js";
2
3 export function filterSessions(sessions: Session[], since?: Date): Session[] {
4   if (since === undefined) {
5     return sessions;
6   }
7   return sessions.filter((session) => session.startedAt.getTime() >= since.getTime());
8 }
```

`src/cli/sessions.ts` (changed, lines 14-19):
```ts
14   .command("list")
15   .option("--since <date>", "Only sessions started on or after this date")
16   .action((opts: { since?: string }) => {
17     const since = opts.since === undefined ? undefined : new Date(opts.since);
18     print(formatSessions(filterSessions(loadSessions(), since)));
19   });
```

`src/sessions/__tests__/filter.test.ts` (added):
```ts
1 import { expect, test } from "bun:test";
2 import { filterSessions } from "../filter.js";
3
4 const sessions = [
5   { id: "a", startedAt: new Date("2026-09-10T08:00:00Z") },
6   { id: "b", startedAt: new Date("2026-09-12T08:00:00Z") },
7   { id: "c", startedAt: new Date("2026-09-14T08:00:00Z") },
8 ];
9
10 test("without --since every session is listed", () => {
11   expect(filterSessions(sessions).map((s) => s.id)).toEqual(["a", "b", "c"]);
12 });
13
14 test("--since keeps a session that started exactly at the cutoff", () => {
15   const since = new Date("2026-09-10T08:00:00Z");
16   expect(filterSessions(sessions, since).map((s) => s.id)).toEqual(["a", "b", "c"]);
17 });
```

